159
00:09:57,970 --> 00:10:02,030
or ROA, in a database.

160
00:10:02,520 --> 00:10:11,090
Then some software called a
validator that runs in an AS.

161
00:10:11,090 --> 00:10:17,880
Deploying RPKI, downloads
all of the ROAs or ROAs,

162
00:10:17,880 --> 00:10:20,930
and verifies the signatures.

163
00:10:20,930 --> 00:10:24,220
At this point when
we say the AS,

164
00:10:24,220 --> 00:10:27,370
so all of the networks, ideally,

165
00:10:27,370 --> 00:10:29,860
but whichever one
chooses to say, hey,

166
00:10:29,860 --> 00:10:32,890
I want to protect the network,

167
00:10:32,890 --> 00:10:37,400
I want to upgrade
